Secrets Engine - Dynamic Secrets
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the concept of dynamic secrets and their advantages over static secrets
Configure HashiCorp Vault to generate dynamic secrets for AWS RDS databases
Set up and configure the AWS secrets engine in Vault
Create database connections and roles for dynamic secret generation
Generate and test dynamic database credentials
Verify the lifecycle management of dynamic secrets including automatic rotation and revocation
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with database concepts and SQL
Basic knowledge of AWS services, particularly RDS
Understanding of HashiCorp Vault fundamentals
Experience with JSON configuration files
Basic networking concepts
